Today I solved leetcode question 3727: Maximum alternating sum of squares

Description: It states that we are given an array of integers.
              We must arrange them in such a way that when we add squares of numbers at even index and subtract squares of nums at odd index we must get maximum sum.
              eg- array=[1,2,3]
                  ans=12 we can arrange like [2,1,3]

Solution: As we are taking squares of the numbers so their initial sign does not matter.
          First we convert all the negative integers to positive numbers.
          Then we sort the whole array.
          Now we create three variables named i,j and answer.
          i and answer will have value as 0 and j will have value of last index of our array.
          Then we will start our while loop which will run till i is less than equal to j.
          First we add square of number at index j to our answer.
          Then we check if i is equal to j or not. If yes then we will break our loop.
          Now we will subtract square of number from answer.
          At last we will increase i by 1 and decrease j by 1.
